  "worked_solution": "First, we find the value of the function at $P$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(4,2,1) & ={4}^{2}+3(2-1)^{2}-{1}^{2}=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that the level surfaces for the function $f(x,y,z)$ are given by the equation\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=c.\n$$\n\nIn our case, we're interested in $c=18.$ So, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & =c \\\\ {x}^{2}+3(y-1)^{2}-{z}^{2} & =18 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the level surface that passes through the point $P(4,2,1)$ is the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{18}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{18}=1.$",
